n (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Greg Landsman, the Democratic incumbent, enters the final stretch favored to hold a Cincinnati-area seat that leans slightly Republican. Polls from late October show him ahead of Eric Conroy by roughly two to nine points, and he has raised more than twice as much money as his challenger. Republican committees and outside groups have spent heavily against him, but reports indicate national Republicans pulled funding from the district as analysts moved the race toward Democrats.\n\nNine of ten expert ratings call the race Likely Democratic, with one rating it Tilt Democratic, and prediction markets mostly price Democratic odds above 95 percent. Conroy has kept the race competitive on the airwaves with outside help, and an attack line about Landsman's investment in a China-linked fund has circulated late. Even so, the combination of incumbency, money, and polling leads points to a Democratic hold with moderate uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8451, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8473, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8639, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8273, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7978, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.84, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.87, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8688, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8815, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8538, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 7.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8433, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.866, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8525, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8683, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8513, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "202